# phlix-website response headers — READ THE HOST REALITY FIRST
#
# HOST CAVEAT: this site deploys to GitHub Pages (.github/workflows/pages.yml
# uploads dist/ with actions/upload-pages-artifact and deploys to the
# github-pages environment). GitHub Pages IGNORES this file — it has no
# custom-response-header mechanism. The directives below apply ONLY when the
# origin is fronted by a headers-supporting host (Cloudflare Pages/Workers,
# nginx, Apache, ...). The file is kept deliberately: it is the exact config to
# activate on such a host, and it changes nothing while the host is GitHub.
#
# WHAT ACTUALLY SHIPS TODAY: tools/build.mjs injects the Content-Security-
# Policy <meta> form of this policy into EVERY page in dist/ — the only CSP
# delivery GitHub Pages honors. Single source of truth: tools/csp.mjs; the CSP
# line below is pinned byte-equal to it by test/csp-gate.test.mjs (law 2).
#
# Why each allowance exists (measured on the built tree, 2026-10-29):
# - script-src 'unsafe-inline': the root gallery and 404 shim run inline
#   scripts (the build injects the kit manifest; both pages have hand-authored
#   inline logic) and 8 kit pages carry inline <script>/onclick islands. A
#   strict script-src 'self' would disable the site it claims to protect — the
#   previous "no unsafe-inline for scripts" note was never achievable here.
# - style-src 'unsafe-inline': 497 shipped pages carry inline style= attributes
#   and 43 carry inline <style> blocks. (The old note said "322 inline style=
#   attributes across variants"; the variants/ tree was deleted 2026-06-30.)
# - https://fonts.googleapis.com / fonts.gstatic.com: ONLY the root gallery's
#   stylesheet loads from Google. Every kit site self-hosts its woff2 under
#   shared/assets/fonts/ (tools/vendor-fonts.mjs).
# - frame-ancestors 'self' (NOT 'none'): the gallery previews each kit by
#   framing <slug>/index.html same-origin; 'none' killed the site's own
#   feature. X-Frame-Options mirrors this as SAMEORIGIN (DENY framed the same
#   contradiction).
#
# HOST-CONFIG TODO — what GitHub Pages CANNOT deliver, even with this file in
# dist/: the three response headers below (X-Content-Type-Options,
# X-Frame-Options, Referrer-Policy) and the CSP's own frame-ancestors
# directive (browsers ignore frame-ancestors inside a meta tag). They go live
# only once a headers-capable front (Cloudflare Pages/Workers, nginx, ...)
# serves this file — owner decision: front the Pages site or move hosts.
#
# No CSP violation-report endpoint exists in this repo (none is wired).

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
